id: pm-slack-s53m
title: Keep outbox opt-in and recovery policy atomic across crashes
description: "Overlap recheck: durable Slack delivery is already shipped by PR 147 and tracked by pm-slack-3e7d. Core CLI owns verified item history and lifecycle commits, not Slack delivery; pm-observer owns evidence-note delivery; pm-slack-standup owns digests; immediate Slack retry/backoff remains transport logic. This follow-up addresses a separate crash window between durable opt-in and its eligibility snapshot, without rebuilding existing capabilities."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-23T19:31:03.630Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-23T19:35:03.883Z"
assignee: codex-agent
claim_principal: codex-agent
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Crash/retry fixtures produce one acknowledged send; ambiguous remote outcomes remain visible; notification failure never rolls back a committed item. A crash while enabling never leaves opt-in without its initial policy. Typed SDK and CLI, bounded TOON/JSON, typed remedies, README/example, non-git real tracker validation and unchanged npm/Bun CI gates remain verified."
comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-23T19:31:24.983Z",codex-agent,"Plan: reuse shipped SlackOutbox, captureSlackOutbox, registered CLI and SDK verified history/replay. Make enable persist opt-in and its first recovery policy in one SQLite transaction. Exercise real process death between writes plus a real SQLite policy-write refusal, then recover a later SDK lifecycle and acknowledge it exactly once. Existing feature pm-slack-3e7d remains the original delivery scope; this item owns the newly identified atomic-enable gap."
  "2026-10-23T19:34:15.602Z",codex-agent,"Implementation: enable now fences opt-in plus initial eligibility with BEGIN IMMEDIATE/COMMIT and rolls both back on a policy-write error, returning storage_unavailable with an enable remedy. Behavioral revert proof: restoring only origin/main enable made both new atomic-enable tests fail (raw SQLite refusal; persisted timestamp after child exit 73 instead of null). Restored code passes 36 outbox tests with zero failures/skips/cancellations. Typecheck, build, test compilation, docstring lint (82 declarations) and native Bun acceptance pass. No standalone lint script exists."
  "2026-10-23T19:34:17.347Z",codex-agent,"Real-data validation: read-only archive of public unbraind/pm-slack origin/main 0e3c084; non-git scratch tracker, git-free PATH and git ceiling. Complete SDK read: 86 items, 642 verified history entries, 179 fingerprinted read-only source files. Recovery queued 0 pre-enable events. Derived 86 snapshot intents, reopened SQLite, acknowledged 86 localhost POSTs; reopened and drained again with 0 duplicates. Source file changes: 0. Bounded inspection returned 10 rows and explicitly omitted 76. Localhost sinks only; no live Slack delivery claimed."
  "2026-10-23T19:35:03.883Z",codex-agent,"All four linked commands passed via pm test --run --progress --timeout 300: outbox suite 36 passed; typecheck passed; docstring lint 82 declarations; native Bun one recovered event, one acknowledgment, zero duplicates. Existing project policy disables persisted linked-run receipts (tracking_disabled); measured results are retained here without changing policy. Full unchanged npm and Bun release gates will run in the CI Node 22/26 matrix."
